From 7c0f038ea7980792e3d16d1b6cdc29c29e13a4cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:59:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/42] drm/gma500: check the SGX545 transfer queue waits on
 syncs

Let dummy transfers carry a destination sync, and add dri/N/sgx/xfer_sync: a
transfer whose sync is one write short must stay queued, and once the host
completes the write and sends PROCESS_QUEUES it must run. The EDM then moves
the destination's write counter past its pending value and leaves its read
counter alone. The GMA3600 behaves exactly so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
---
